{"additions":135,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nCloses #163.\n\n- **Limit-aware fetching** — GraphQL cost scales with the *requested* `--limit` (measured: `item-list --limit 500` ≈ 101 pt, `field-list --limit 100` ≈ 101 pt, everything else ~0). `field-list` now asks for 30 and `item-list` for 100 first; a single re-fetch at the old limits (100 / 500) happens only when the first page came back full and `totalCount` says more exists (`needs_bigger_fetch`). A typical board fetch drops from **~200 to ~50 points**; a vig left on the Projects page goes from ~2,400 to ~600 points/hour.\n- **Quota visibility** — the views query piggy-backs `rateLimit { remaining }` (cost-free); the Projects status bar shows `⚠ api N left` when fewer than 1,500 of the hourly 5,000 points remain (red below 500). Not cached — the figure always comes from a live response.\n- Guide (en/ja): the Projects constraints describe the two-step fetch and the warning; Troubleshooting notes that a forgotten Projects-page instance quietly spends points all day.\n\n## Tests\n\n`needs_bigger_fetch` covers under-full pages, full pages with/without a reported total, and the at-max case. 366 tests green, clippy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":9,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-07T07:29:08Z","deletions":13,"headRefName":"feat/projects-api-cost","labels":[],"number":164,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMbmldw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\n`ProjectsState.api_remaining` can remain stale when a board update has `api_remaining: None` (e.g., disk-cached board or views fetch failure), causing misleading low-quota warnings.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR reduces GitHub GraphQL point consumption for the Projects board fetch by doing limit-aware two-step fetching, and surfaces remaining GraphQL quota in the Projects status bar when it runs low.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add two-step fetching for `gh project item-list` (100 → 500) and `gh project field-list` (30 → 100) using `needs_bigger_fetch` to avoid high-cost large limits for small boards.\n- Piggy-back `rateLimit { remaining }` onto the views GraphQL query and plumb `api_remaining` through `Board` → `ProjectsState` → status bar to warn when quota is low.\n- Update English/Japanese guide and troubleshooting docs to describe the new fetching strategy and quota warning.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/projects/state.rs | Stores latest `api_remaining` from board fetch results for status bar display. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/types.rs | Adds non-cached `Board.api_remaining` (serde-skipped) for quota reporting. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/disk_cache.rs | Updates cache tests to account for the new `Board` field. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/client.rs | Implements limit-aware two-step fetching and returns `(views, api_remaining)` from views query; adds unit tests for `needs_bigger_fetch`. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Renders low-quota warning `⚠ api N left` with threshold-based coloring. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-projects.md | Documents two-step fetch and the quota warning behavior. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/troubleshooting.md | Notes Projects page can burn points over time and references the new warning. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md | Japanese documentation updates mirroring the English Projects constraints. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/troubleshooting.md | Japanese troubleshooting updates mirroring the English quota warning note. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 9/9 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T07:31:56Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"14e9a289e18ccf2633ed1c511102bab66dbc8917"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMbp5bw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T07:37:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"14e9a289e18ccf2633ed1c511102bab66dbc8917"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T07:38:36Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34096471830/job/101661158561","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-09-07T07:38:42Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T07:32:54Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34095693374/job/101658742932","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-07T07:29:15Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T07:29:40Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34095693407/job/101658743107","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-09-07T07:29:14Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T07:32:20Z","conclusion"